<title>CANADA: Canada eliminates import quotas on men's shirts.</title>
<headline>Canada eliminates import quotas on men's shirts.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada has eliminated import quotas on tailored collar shirts, Finance Minister Paul Martin said on Friday.</p>
<p>But Canada will provide Canadian shirt manufacturers with transitional assistance until the end of 2004 to help them deal with the quota elimination, since the Canadian industry has traditionally been sensitive to low-cost imports, Martin said in a statement.</p>
<p>The men's shirt industry in Canada has production worth about C$160 million a year. Canada must eliminate the import quotas as part of its obligations under the North American Free Trade Agreement, the official said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613 235-6745))</p>
</text>
